    TEST-0002: test each level: core, adapters, and end to end
    
    The core's tests (rules.spec.ts and BookingDesk.spec.ts) are unit
    tests: no file, and at most a FakeBookingStore. They say nothing about
    whether JsonBookingStore works, or whether a passing test against the
    fake means anything for the real store.
    
    bookingStoreContract.ts is what every BookingStore promises, written
    once. FakeBookingStore.spec.ts and adapters/JsonBookingStore.spec.ts
    both run it. The JSON run is an integration test: a real store, a real
    file in a fresh temp directory, and no core. It has two more tests
    only a file can fail: a second store sees the first one's bookings,
    and the file is in the format Facilities reads.
    
    The contract caught a bug on its first run. A JsonBookingStore whose
    file doesn't exist yet threw ENOENT instead of having no bookings, so
    the very first booking on a new machine would have crashed. The fake
    can't have that bug, and no core test could see it. The adapter now
    treats a missing file as no bookings.
    
    e2e.spec.ts goes in the front door: run() with argv, the real core, and
    a real JsonBookingStore on a temp file. Each command gets a new store,
    the way each yarn start does. There are only two tests, because the
    rules are already covered below: these check that the pieces are wired
    together.

